.Fn ble_read_battery "ble_ctx_t *ctx" "const ble_addr_t *addr" "ble_read_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm libble
library provides a callback-driven C API for Bluetooth Low Energy
operations.
It communicates with the
.Xr blued 8
daemon over its Unix domain control socket, abstracting the text
protocol into typed function calls with asynchronous event delivery.
.Pp
The design is similar in spirit to Apple's CoreBluetooth framework:
applications open a context, register callbacks for events of interest,
and drive event dispatch by calling
.Fn ble_process
when the socket is readable.
.Pp
.Fn ble_open
connects to the blued control socket.
If
.Fa sock_path
is
.Dv NULL ,
the default path
.Pa /var/run/blued.sock
is used.
Returns an opaque context, or
.Dv NULL
on failure.
.Pp
.Fn ble_fd
returns the socket file descriptor for integration with
.Xr poll 2 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
or
.Xr select 2 .
.Pp
.Fn ble_process
reads available data from the daemon and dispatches any pending
callbacks.
Returns 0 on success, or \-1 if the connection was lost.
.Pp
.Fn ble_scan
initiates a BLE scan.
Discovered devices are reported via the
.Fa cb
callback, one invocation per device.
.Pp
.Fn ble_connect
initiates a connection to the specified device.
The
.Fa cb
callback is invoked when the connection succeeds or fails.
.Pp
.Fn ble_discover
runs GATT service and characteristic discovery on a connected device.
Results are delivered to the
.Fa cb
callback.
.Pp
.Fn ble_read
and
.Fn ble_write
perform GATT characteristic read and write operations.
.Pp
.Fn ble_subscribe
registers for characteristic value change notifications.
The
.Fa cb
callback fires for each notification received.
.Pp
.Fn ble_add_service
and related peripheral-mode functions allow building a local GATT
server.
.Pp
.Fn ble_read_battery
is a convenience function that auto-discovers the Battery Service
(UUID 0x180F) and reads the Battery Level characteristic.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Scan for nearby BLE devices:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <ble.h>
#include <poll.h>
#include <stdio.h>

static void
on_device(const ble_scan_result_t *r, void *arg)
{
    char buf[18];
    printf("Found: %s rssi=%d name=%s\\n",
        ble_addr_str(&r->addr, buf), r->rssi, r->name);
}

int
main(void)
{
    ble_ctx_t *ctx = ble_open(NULL);
    struct pollfd pfd;

    ble_scan(ctx, on_device, NULL);

    pfd.fd = ble_fd(ctx);
    pfd.events = POLLIN;
    while (poll(&pfd, 1, 10000) > 0)
        ble_process(ctx);

    ble_close(ctx);
    return (0);
}
